---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { loadSiteContent } from '../lib/content';

const { showNotes } = await loadSiteContent();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Don Yuen: a computer science graduate who builds LLM applications, evaluates their output, and knows the math underneath."
  showNotes={showNotes}
>
  <div class="page prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I'm Don Yuen, a computer science graduate building toward AI engineering.
      I care most about whether a model's output can be trusted.
    </p>
    <p>
      My Historic Photo Explorer is a Node.js app that finds Library of Congress
      photos and asks Claude to describe them for blind and low-vision readers.
      It requests JSON-schema structured outputs and escapes everything the
      model returns before it reaches the page. To judge the descriptions, I
      wrote a rubric, had four other models grade them blind, and hand-checked
      every score where they disagreed by two points or more. That evaluation
      found the real failure: 150 px thumbnails. Fixing it lifted accuracy on
      those photos from 3.4 to 4.6.
    </p>
    <p>
      I also wanted to understand training underneath the frameworks. With an AI
      coding assistant, I built a 784-128-64-10 network in NumPy and derived
      backpropagation by hand. I swept learning rate, width, and batch size
      across three seeds before choosing settings, and it reached 98.32% test
      accuracy.
    </p>

    <h2>Skills I use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>LLM application work:</strong> the Claude API, structured
        outputs, and prompt design driven by evaluation results.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Evaluation:</strong> rubrics, model-as-judge panels, agreement
        checks against human scores, and clear limits on what a score means.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>ML fundamentals:</strong> backpropagation, gradient checking,
        and controlled experiments across seeds.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Shipping:</strong> TypeScript, Python, Node.js, and automated
        tests with CI. I build with AI coding assistants and review and test
        their code.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>I'm looking for AI engineering roles.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lede {
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: clamp(21px, 3.4vw, 26px);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
</style>
